{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/lme-seed-launch-params.json.j2 -- the launch-params EXPORT
    (controller.bootstrap.seed_launcher.params_rel; codex 211754 / 212700 / 213721 / 214135). Input (a declaration, never
    an extra-var of desired state): lme_seed_bs = profile remote_harness.controller.bootstrap. Output: ONE JSON object
    {<mode>: [<mode parameter name>, ...]} for every seed_launch.mode_args mode (dictsort order), each list EXACTLY the
    canonical macro launch_params of that mode's words -- the positional parameters the generated launcher takes after
    <root> (seed_launcher.caller_argv {mode_params}). A thin call: no second classifier of placeholder words.
    Rendered only through the template lookup (G's controls); nothing executes it; NOT a bundle member.
    Import: the declared relationship of the two profile paths (macros_rel relative to the directory of params_rel).
    The layout is validated at RESOLVE, before any render, by the loader (lme_manifests.py _rh_prove_artifact_templates /
    _rh_bind_declared_import: both values normalized relative paths, params_rel == shared_artifacts.launcher_params
    templates[0], the import target strictly inside the entry directory and a declared non-entry template; contract
    bootstrap_macros pins macros_rel to the registry); anything else refuses at resolve, with no fallback import path.
    Filters: Jinja builtins only (dictsort, string, tojson) plus relpath / dirname inside the import operand only
    (IMPORT-STATIC-FILTER-KNOWLEDGE, codex 214135). tojson escapes < > & ' as \u00XX: still JSON. No trailing newline
    in this file, so the rendered export carries none on either toolchain. -#}
{%- import lme_seed_bs.macros_rel | relpath(lme_seed_bs.seed_launcher.params_rel | dirname) as m -%}
{{ '{' }}
{%- for mode, words in lme_seed_bs.seed_launch.mode_args | dictsort -%}
{{ mode | tojson }}: {{ (m.launch_params(words) | string).split() | tojson }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '' }}
{%- endfor -%}
{{ '}' }}